---
/**
 * Digital Agriculture Information Board — project detail page.
 */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Digital Agriculture Information Board"
  description="An embedded agricultural telemetry and information interface delivering field sensor insights to agricultural operators."
  label="Engineering — Completed"
  heading="Digital Agriculture Information Board"
  subheading="IoT Telemetry & Embedded Display System"
>
  <article class="case-study" aria-label="Project case study">
    <div class="container case-study-grid">
      <div class="case-main">

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-problem">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-problem">The Problem</h2>
          <p>Agricultural operators manage complex field conditions — soil moisture, temperature, humidity, pest risk — that affect yield outcomes. Raw sensor data is often inaccessible to operators without technical expertise, and existing telemetry displays are designed for offices rather than fields.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-why">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-why">Why It Matters</h2>
          <p>Better access to field-level data could help smaller farms make better decisions without expensive proprietary systems. A practical, readable interface is as important as the sensor network behind it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-role">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-role">My Role</h2>
          <p>I designed and built the embedded display interface — responsible for the hardware platform selection, sensor integration, data processing and the visual display logic that translated raw readings into contextually useful information for operators.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-approach">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-approach">Approach</h2>
          <p>The project used a Raspberry Pi as the central processing unit with Python-based sensor polling and display logic. The interface was designed for glanceability — operators needed to read key metrics at a distance, in variable lighting. Early prototypes were tested against readability criteria before the display hierarchy was refined.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-outcome">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-outcome">Outcome</h2>
          <p>A working embedded display prototype that pulled from multiple sensors and presented contextually structured data. Key learning: the interface design was as critical as the electronics — operators engaged far more with the visual display than with raw data logs.</p>
        </section>

      </div>
      <aside class="case-meta" aria-label="Project details">
        <div class="case-meta-card">
          <dl class="case-meta-list">
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Type</dt><dd>Embedded Systems Project</dd></div>
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Status</dt><dd>Completed</dd></div>
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Raspberry Pi</dd></div>
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Tools</dt><dd>Python, Raspberry Pi, Tkinter, IoT sensors</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="case-meta-tags">
            {['Embedded Systems', 'IoT', 'Telemetry', 'Hardware', 'Python'].map(t => (
              <span class="tag">{t}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}work/`} class="back-link">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="19" y1="12" x2="5" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 19 5 12 12 5"/>
          </svg>
          All projects
        </a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

